Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Additive changes so configs can express every practical OpenAPI fact
(motivated by zopia's code generation):

- methodSchema: accept trace/TRACE/Trace (all 8 standard methods)
- response keys: any custom numeric status code (419, 499, 512, ...) and
  the OpenAPI 'default' key, alongside standard codes (number/string form)
  — mapped literal union ∩ numeric index signature ∩ optional default;
  arbitrary string keys still rejected (tsc --strict verified)
- IResponseContentType / IRequestContentType: open string unions — any
  MIME accepted, known values still autocompleted; runtime schemas
  unchanged (still validate the known set)
- contentTypeCategory: general '+json' suffix rule (application/vnd.*+json
  → json); unknown types fall back to text as before
- new optional operationId field (+ IOperationId export)

No migration required — every change is a superset of accepted values.
9 new tests (170 total), tsc clean.
