+## v0.4.0 — Open response keys, TRACE & open content types
+
+### What changed
+
+Four additive changes so endpoint configs can express **every** practical
+OpenAPI fact (motivated by zopia's code generation — every generated
+`index.ts` must fill all practical API content):
+
+#### 1. `TRACE` is a valid method
+
+`methodSchema` now accepts `trace` / `TRACE` / `Trace` alongside the other
+seven methods (case-insensitive, as before).
+
+#### 2. Open response keys
+
+`response` accepts, in addition to the standard status codes (number or
+string form, unchanged):
+
+- **any other numeric status code** — `419`, `427`, `444`, `499`, `509`,
+  `512`, … (e.g. Laravel's `419`, nginx's `499`);
+- the **`default`** key — the OpenAPI "default" response.
+
+The type is built as a mapped literal union (standard codes, with full
+autocomplete) intersected with a numeric index signature and an optional
+`default` property — so standard-code keys still autocomplete, any numeric
+code is accepted, and arbitrary string keys are still rejected:
+
+```ts
+type ResponseMap<T> = {
+  [K in IHttpStatusCode | `${IHttpStatusCode}`]?: T;
+} & { [k: number]: T | undefined } & { default?: T };
+```
+
+#### 3. Open content types
+
+`IResponseContentType` / `IRequestContentType` are now open string unions —
+**any** MIME type is accepted, with the known values still autocompleted
+(`OpenStringUnion<T> = T | (string & {})`).
+
+The runtime schema values (`responseContentTypeSchema`,
+`requestContentTypeSchema`) are **unchanged** — they still validate only the
+known set, for consumers who want strict runtime validation.
+
+Adapter behaviour for arbitrary types (previously unreachable through the
+type system, now reachable):
+
+- `contentTypeCategory` gained a general `+json` suffix rule, so
+  `application/vnd.custom+json` and `application/geo+json` map to `json`;
+- everything else falls back to `text` (charset extraction still applies).
+
+#### 4. `operationId`
+
+New optional `operationId` field on the config (and `IOperationId` type
+export) — the OpenAPI operationId, unique across the document, used by docs
+tools and code generators (e.g. zopia). Returned unchanged by
+`makeApiConfig`.
+
+### Migration
+
+**None required** — every change is a superset of the previously accepted
+values. Existing configs compile and behave exactly as before.
+
+### Type-level proof
+
+The response-key shape was verified with `tsc --strict`: standard codes
+(numeric/string), custom numeric codes (including their string forms),
+`default`, and empty objects are accepted; arbitrary string keys are
+rejected.
+
+---
+
